ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Agesilao treated with his ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Agesilao 
treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Agesilao treated with his ally Kahn 
(#6).  Agesilao treated with his ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).
  Stormy winter gave way to spring, and Agesilao prepared to carry out his 
imperial orders.  He prepared his armies to defend Bizerte and the 
surrounding provinces.
  With the coming of the early summer season Agesilao practiced his Tactics 
for months, but could make no significant headway.
  In late summer, Agesilao practiced his Tactics well, and even consulted an 
astrologer, but could not improve his Tactics.
  The summer surrendered to fall.  Agesilao boldly marched his command into 
Bizerte (#1807).
  With the coming of the early winter season, Agesilao cast a Bless spell.  
The Argyre Sea was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no 
armies in the Argyre Sea.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Agesilao for this year.


  Agesilao treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Agesilao treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).
Agesilao treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Kahn (#6).  Agesilao treated with his ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  
Agesilao treated with his ally Circe (#8).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Astelle (#82) heard that an old friend was trapping furs in Katmai and 
left the First Sea to see her old friend.


  Here is the financial report for Agesilao's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 51 gold in revenue.  7 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  34 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Agesilao was left 
with 31 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Tancred
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I rode my flying armies into the Arrak Sea.

  Agesilao's minions initiated a campaign of conquest directed at the Arrak 
Sea, a Sea province owing allegiance to Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0).  I commanded the attacking fleet.  The defenders were commanded by 
Lakes (#64).  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

