  DEFENDING ARMY

  I led my navies into the fray.  Standing at the ready with his ships was 
Lakes.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Babba Sissoko (#0) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Lakes (#64) stepped forward and challenged me to personal 
combat.  I declined to enter personal combat.
  The forces commanded by me were dismayed by my cowardice.  They marched 
on, though with lessened confidence.  The opposing forces raced to be 
upwind, and I obtained an advantage by arriving there first.  But my 
meticulous tactical maneuvers did not work out as expected, and my forces 
entered battle with a slight tactical disadvantage.

  On the left outside wing, the 161st Eagles were arrayed against the 266th 
Whales.  The 161st Eagles soared over the 266th Whales and attacked without 
mercy.  The 266th Whales swam underwater and attacked.  The 161st Eagles 
fought the 266th Whales and were knocked out of the fight by the enemy's 
ferocious attack.
  In the interior lines, the Green 14th Eagles were arrayed against the 
111th Fleet Marines.  The 14th Eagles soared over the 111th Fleet Marines 
and attacked without mercy.  The 164th Skeletal Mermen swam underwater and 
attacked.  The 14th Eagles fought the 111th Fleet Marines and were sliced 
and diced like a knife cutting through lard.
  Out on the right outside wing, the Veteran 195th Phalanx faced the Veteran 
73rd Whales.  The 73rd Whales swam undersea and attacked.  The 195th Phalanx 
fought with the 73rd Whales and had their booties kicked up their throats.
  Having found a weak spot in the line of the armada of Agesilao, a final 
determined slashing attack defeated their opponent and won the day for Lakes.
The 266th Whales scattered the 161st Eagles in all directions.  The 111th 
Fleet Marines demolished the 14th Eagles.  The 73rd Whales destroyed the 
195th Phalanx.
  The armada of the attacking Kingdom was defeated and forced out of the 
Arrak Sea.  My forces completely dispersed, I fled alone to Mare Ritalis.
  Midsummer's night passed and late summer arrived.  I attempted an illegal 
move.  I tried to move from Mare Ritalis to the Mariner Sea, a non-adjacent 
province.  Instead, I travelled to the Arrak Sea.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into the fall.  I could not cast Plague 
on Silvania because I needed to be in or next to the target province.  
Instead, I discovered nothing in my sagely researches.
  In early winter, I attempted an illegal move.  I tried to move from the 
Arrak Sea to the Orca Sea, a non-adjacent province.  Instead, I journeyed to 
Mare Serenitus.

  Thy humble servant,   Tancred


From: Montgomery, Squire to Negumba
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter melted into sweet spring.  Negumba practiced his Druidism 
well, and even consulted a palm reader, but could not improve his Druidism.
  With the coming of the early summer season Negumba was instructed in 
Tactics by Agesilao.  Negumba practiced for months and his skill in Tactics 
increased.  He conducted tactical exercises and the 136th Warg Riders 
improved in quality.
  In late summer, Negumba was instructed in Tactics by Agesilao.  Negumba 
practiced his Tactics and his skill in Tactics went up.
  The summer surrendered to the fall.  Negumba moved into Mare Frigidis 
(#1708) with his army.
  With the advent of the early winter season, Negumba worked hard on his 
Tactics but was thwarted in his self-improvement efforts.

  Thy humble servant,   Montgomery, Squire to Negumba


From: Stonebrick
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I was instructed in the art of Druidism by Negumba.  I 
rehearsed and practiced my Druidism and improved noticeably.
  Windy spring blossomed into a sultry early summer.  I was tutored in 
Tactics by Agesilao.  I practiced well and improved my skill in Tactics.
  With the coming of the late summer season I moved into the Seahorse Sea.  
Turning to the west, one can see a Forest area, which is known as the 
Atlantis Sea (#1507).  It is populated by Elves and Bouticca rules there.  
Their Elven fighters traditionally array themselves in the style of Bowmen 
and Fleet.  To the northwest lies a Sea area called the Giant Crab Sea 
(#1506), populated by no races.  It is ruled by 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango.  While adventuring, I encountered no 
monster.
  In fall, I rode into the Atlantis Sea.  Southwest of here lies the 
province of the Orca Sea (#1408), ruled by Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango. 
It is known to be a Sea province inhabited by no races.  Viewing the western 
horizon, a man can see a prosperous Sea province known as the Stonegard Sea 
(#1407).  It is said that Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango is the ruler 
there.  It is known to be occupied by Mermen.  If need be, they can call on 
an army of Mermen to defend their province.  To the northwest there lies a 
Forest province known as the Plesiosaurus Sea (#1406), a poor land of Elves 
where Kurtinaitis reigns.  Their Elven fighters traditionally fight in the 
style of Bowmen and Chariots.  I saw no monsters.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  I travelled to the Orca Sea.  
Southwest of here is the Mariner Sea (#1409), a Mountain area owned by 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango, where Orcs dwell.  Their Orcish warriors 
traditionally fight as Axemen.  Looking to the west, one can see a rich 
Mountain area, which is known as Silvania (#1308).  It is populated by Elves 
and Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango rules there.  Their Elven fighters 
prefer to array themselves in the style of Bowmen and Fleet.  While 
adventuring, I saw no monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Stonebrick


